"failure_policy":{"action":"stop","retries":1,"skip_on_empty_port":false,"tolerance":null},"input_ports":[{"params":{},"port_id":"rules","port_type":"rules","window":"all"},{"params":{},"port_id":"problem","port_type":"problem","window":"all"}],"instruction":"Build two texts. \"input\" is any reply text you like; \"rewritten\" is a second text, different from the first, changed however you judge most informative. Say what the RULE AS WRITTEN says the check's answer ought to do between them: \"moves\" or \"unchanged\". Quote the words you read it from in the body.\n\nA kernel id may instead be written open:creib.forge.conformance.<module>.<function>, naming any function of one string in one of these modules of the harness under test. No list of functions is given: read the source and choose. A function that raises on a text has not answered, and a pair on which either side raised is not a move.\n\n- creib.forge.conformance.appraisal\n- creib.forge.conformance.claims\n- creib.forge.conformance.compare\n- creib.forge.conformance.controls\n- creib.forge.conformance.corpus\n- creib.forge.conformance.cycles\n- creib.forge.conformance.dependence\n- creib.forge.conformance.families\n- creib.forge.conformance.oracle\n- creib.forge.conformance.prompt\n- creib.forge.conformance.records\n- creib.forge.conformance.report\n- creib.forge.conformance.routing\n- creib.forge.conformance.spec\n- creib.forge.conformance.units\n\nThe commitments are a STRING holding JSON of the form {\"kernel\": \"<id>\", \"expect\": \"moves\" or \"unchanged\"} and nothing else; this artifact carries \"input\", \"rewritten\" and \"rewrite\" as fields of its own, each a plain string. Do not repeat a pair already proposed.","kind_id":"mini.pair-proposal.sweep.v1","optional_fields":["input","rewritten","rewrite"],"output_port":{"port_id":"out","produces_kind":"mini.pair-proposal.sweep.v1"},"title":"Propose"},{"commitment_call":"two","commitment_ports":[],"failure_policy":{"action":"stop","retries":1,"skip_